<main>
  <section class="page-section">
    <div class="container">
      <div class="d-flex align-items-center gap-3 flex-wrap">
        <h1 class="section-title mb-0">Program</h1>
        <span class="badge-tbd">Provisional &mdash; full schedule to follow</span>
      </div>
      <p class="lead" style="max-width: 48rem;">
        A full-day, Dagstuhl-style (&ldquo;Barstuhl&rdquo;) workshop: discussion-driven,
        not a paper track. The shape below reflects the accepted proposal; exact timings
        will be finalized closer to the workshop day. 
        A Zotero group will be created for collaborative bibliography management. 
      </p>

      <ol class="list-group list-group-numbered mb-4" style="max-width: 48rem;">
        <li class="list-group-item card-mkg mb-3 border-0">
          <strong>Plenary pitch session</strong> &middot; ~90 minutes<br>
          Selected lightning pitches balancing the theoretical/logician and
          engineering/database perspectives.
        </li>
        <li class="list-group-item card-mkg mb-3 border-0">
          <strong>Breakout working sessions</strong> &middot; ~180 minutes<br>
          Three parallel pillars &mdash; (a) Reference Use Cases, (b) Engineering
          Challenges, (c) Foundational Models (see <a href="index.html#research">Research
          questions</a>) &mdash; run as three 60-minute rounds with participant
          reshuffling; each group drafts sections of the community document.
        </li>
        <li class="list-group-item card-mkg border-0">
          <strong>Alignment &amp; synthesis plenary</strong> &middot; 60&ndash;90 minutes<br>
          Reconcile breakout outputs, resolve friction, and set the roadmap and writing
          assignments for the White Paper.
        </li>
      </ol>

      <p style="max-width: 48rem;">
        Exact timings and room assignment will be finalized closer to the workshop day
        (25 or 26 October 2026, exact day assigned by the ISWC chairs).
      </p>
    </div>
  </section>
</main>

